+rsomics-vcf concat -a -r chr1:1-1000000 chunk-a.vcf.gz chunk-b.vcf.gz
+```
+
+Ligation reconciles complete phased diploid heterozygous genotypes across a
+chunk handoff and writes typed PQ and PS values. Each indexed chunk may contain
+records from one contig; separate files can advance to later contigs. Default
+ligation requires a perfect overlap, while `--ligate-warn` drops and reports
+unpaired overlap sites and `--ligate-force` retains them or permits disjoint
+chunks.
+
+Validated naive mode copies compatible BGZF VCF or BCF record frames without
+recompression. It rejects mixed encodings, incompatible headers or BCF
+dictionaries, malformed frames, CRC failures, missing canonical EOF blocks,
+and trailing bytes. Named output is transactional in every mode, and JSON
+summaries require a separate named variant destination.
